1
00:00:05,068 --> 00:00:08,404
I am the granddaughter of the late Nobuko.

2
00:00:08,988 --> 00:00:11,199
Oh, Ms. Nobuko.

3
00:00:12,033 --> 00:00:13,451
Let me carry that.

4
00:00:14,035 --> 00:00:14,994
Mr. Nishigami.

5
00:00:19,666 --> 00:00:20,792
Mr. Nishigami!

6
00:00:22,544 --> 00:00:23,962
See you tomorrow!

7
00:00:25,672 --> 00:00:28,591
<i>At the end of summer,</i>
<i>this villa ground will be hit</i>

8
00:00:28,675 --> 00:00:31,553
<i>by a large-scale landslide</i>
<i>disaster due to a typhoon.</i>

9
00:00:31,636 --> 00:00:35,223
<i>All that's left is to quietly wait</i>
<i>for death at the end of summer.</i>

10
00:00:35,306 --> 00:00:37,183
<i>I think so too, but…</i>

11
00:00:38,268 --> 00:00:41,521
<i>It is forbidden for a Grim Reaper</i>
<i>to feel affection for humans.</i>

12
00:00:41,604 --> 00:00:45,775
<i>You must devote yourself entirely</i>
<i>to witnessing their lifespans.</i>

13
00:00:46,609 --> 00:00:47,610
<i>Understood.</i>

14
00:00:48,278 --> 00:00:49,988
That is my mission, after all.

15
00:00:51,573 --> 00:00:55,410
<i>The </i>Obon <i>holidays started today,</i>
<i>and since this morning,</i>

16
00:00:55,493 --> 00:00:57,495
<i>expressways across Japan</i>
<i>have been congested.</i>

17
00:00:57,579 --> 00:01:01,416
<i>-This is one of those highways.</i>
-<i>Obon </i>holidays, huh.

18
00:01:01,499 --> 00:01:05,170
<i>-The countryside and tourist spots…</i>
-What do we do on <i>Obon </i>again?

19
00:01:05,253 --> 00:01:09,132
Well, it's <i>Obon</i>, but we don't have
anything special to do, right?

20
00:01:09,716 --> 00:01:15,096
Shouldn't we at least visit Midori's
grandma's grave? She built this villa.

21
00:01:19,350 --> 00:01:20,476
What?

22
00:01:21,561 --> 00:01:23,062
What are you saying?

23
00:01:23,146 --> 00:01:24,647
Let's go swimming!

24
00:01:24,731 --> 00:01:26,065
Are you going to the sea?

25
00:01:26,149 --> 00:01:28,985
Yeah! Just earlier,
when I was passing by the beach,

26
00:01:29,068 --> 00:01:31,696
there were hardly any people!
Gosh, that's hot.

27
00:01:31,779 --> 00:01:34,532
-Let's go swimming!
-No way! We don't have our swimsuits!

28
00:01:34,616 --> 00:01:35,992
It's fine! I'm going like this.

29
00:01:36,618 --> 00:01:38,578
It will be fine. Let's go!

30
00:01:38,661 --> 00:01:40,788
You were hiding it with the float…

31
00:01:46,127 --> 00:01:47,420
Who might you be?

32
00:01:50,256 --> 00:01:52,091
Focus!

33
00:02:41,516 --> 00:02:43,434
That's right.

34
00:02:43,518 --> 00:02:46,813
No one had been to this villa for years.

35
00:02:46,896 --> 00:02:50,024
But I heard lots of young people
had been visiting it.

36
00:02:50,108 --> 00:02:55,405
Our temple's supporters told me,
so I came to check things out.

37
00:02:55,488 --> 00:02:59,951
We are the grandchildren of the owner
of this villa. We have the key!

38
00:03:01,327 --> 00:03:02,537
Listen.

39
00:03:03,204 --> 00:03:05,289
The <i>Obon </i>holiday

40
00:03:05,373 --> 00:03:09,127
is not meant for drinking
and playing around.

41
00:03:10,336 --> 00:03:13,548
For Japanese people,
<i>Obon </i>is an annual event,

42
00:03:13,631 --> 00:03:16,050
where we light lanterns,

43
00:03:16,134 --> 00:03:19,804
welcome the spirits
of ancestors back home,

44
00:03:20,555 --> 00:03:22,932
and offer gratitude and memorial services.

45
00:03:23,016 --> 00:03:28,521
It is a solemn and sacred Buddhist event.

46
00:03:29,230 --> 00:03:30,398
Focus!

47
00:03:36,070 --> 00:03:41,868
Nishigami, please teach them
about the various events of <i>Obon</i>.

48
00:03:41,951 --> 00:03:42,952
Sir…

49
00:03:45,496 --> 00:03:49,834
The remains that I left in your care,
are they still…

50
00:03:50,418 --> 00:03:51,377
Oh, right.

51
00:03:51,461 --> 00:03:54,005
Of course, they are safely kept.

52
00:03:57,884 --> 00:03:59,218
About that…

53
00:03:59,302 --> 00:04:02,347
Did the owner of this place
ask you to do that?

54
00:04:03,389 --> 00:04:04,474
Yes.

55
00:04:05,933 --> 00:04:10,229
I was asked to keep a portion
of her ashes near this villa

56
00:04:11,230 --> 00:04:12,357
by the owner.

57
00:04:16,652 --> 00:04:19,447
When were you asked to do that?

58
00:04:20,156 --> 00:04:23,409
Right before she passed away,
or after she passed away?

59
00:04:25,870 --> 00:04:27,288
Right.

60
00:04:27,372 --> 00:04:29,374
She can't ask you after she died, huh.

61
00:04:33,753 --> 00:04:35,213
Focus!

62
00:04:48,142 --> 00:04:51,020
Oh, isn't it here? This looks likely.

63
00:04:51,104 --> 00:04:52,939
This room looks like it has lanterns.

64
00:04:53,022 --> 00:04:55,149
-Right.
-It's packed with so many things.

65
00:04:55,233 --> 00:04:57,568
-Yeah.
-Oh, look, a candle.

66
00:04:57,652 --> 00:04:59,445
You're right.

67
00:05:00,905 --> 00:05:02,240
Come to think of it,

68
00:05:02,323 --> 00:05:04,742
have we ever actually gone to visit
Grandma's grave?

69
00:05:05,535 --> 00:05:08,454
Where would the grave even be?

70
00:05:08,538 --> 00:05:11,916
We hadn't seen Grandma at all
after she remarried, right?

71
00:05:11,999 --> 00:05:16,170
Huh? Did we go to Grandma's funeral?

72
00:05:16,254 --> 00:05:20,258
Yeah, we did go. I sort of remember it.

73
00:05:20,341 --> 00:05:24,387
Oh, could it have been held
at the funeral home here in Tatsumi Town?

74
00:05:25,304 --> 00:05:27,432
I don't remember a single thing.

75
00:05:28,474 --> 00:05:31,686
So, did you come here often
when you were kids?

76
00:05:32,478 --> 00:05:37,441
I only came here once or twice
when I was in early elementary school.

77
00:05:37,525 --> 00:05:38,860
Wait.

78
00:05:38,943 --> 00:05:41,946
But for summer vacation,
we caught insects, right?

79
00:05:42,029 --> 00:05:44,490
We did, right? Huh?

80
00:05:45,324 --> 00:05:48,369
Konta. You remember
what happened yesterday, right?

81
00:05:48,452 --> 00:05:49,370
Yesterday?

82
00:05:49,453 --> 00:05:50,746
Yesterday?

83
00:05:50,830 --> 00:05:52,081
Oh, I…

84
00:05:52,165 --> 00:05:54,959
-My memory might have been erased.
-The heck?

85
00:05:56,460 --> 00:05:59,547
But won't you inherit this villa?

86
00:05:59,630 --> 00:06:00,715
No!

87
00:06:00,798 --> 00:06:05,052
This place belongs to my Grandma's
husband's family. They're rich.

88
00:06:05,136 --> 00:06:09,265
-We are just borrowing the key.
-Yeah.

89
00:06:09,348 --> 00:06:12,310
It's not a lantern, but I found a lamp.

90
00:06:12,393 --> 00:06:14,478
Well, good enough, I guess.

91
00:06:15,062 --> 00:06:16,397
Huh? What is this?

92
00:06:17,023 --> 00:06:19,192
How nostalgic. A Hato Sablés box!

93
00:06:19,275 --> 00:06:20,318
Oh, Hato Sablés!

94
00:06:21,277 --> 00:06:23,779
-What about this lamp?
-What are you doing?

95
00:06:27,325 --> 00:06:29,452
There's a notebook. A diary?

96
00:06:31,495 --> 00:06:33,664
-Wow!
-Oh!

97
00:06:34,165 --> 00:06:36,083
How cute.

98
00:06:36,167 --> 00:06:38,127
Midori, did you draw manga?

99
00:06:38,211 --> 00:06:41,964
-I used to love drawing when I was little.
-I see.

100
00:06:42,048 --> 00:06:44,592
I might have drawn this here
during summer vacation.

101
00:06:44,675 --> 00:06:46,928
Wow, this brings back memories.

102
00:06:47,011 --> 00:06:48,888
I wonder if Grandma kept it for me.

103
00:06:48,971 --> 00:06:50,640
You were actually quite good.

104
00:06:50,723 --> 00:06:52,391
No doubt it's a <i>shoujo </i>manga!

105
00:06:52,475 --> 00:06:55,811
-Right?
-I was copying the manga I liked.

106
00:06:56,604 --> 00:06:58,481
But I had forgotten all about it.

107
00:06:58,564 --> 00:07:01,901
Somehow, when you grow up,
you forget these kinds of things.

108
00:07:02,777 --> 00:07:06,322
-Wait, they are kissing in this one!
-Oh, wow!

109
00:07:07,365 --> 00:07:08,824
Oh, no!

110
00:07:14,497 --> 00:07:16,707
-Grandma's photo!
-I want to see it!

111
00:07:17,750 --> 00:07:18,960
She was a beauty.

112
00:07:19,043 --> 00:07:21,254
Wasn't she way too beautiful?

113
00:07:23,130 --> 00:07:25,132
-How nostalgic.
-She was stylish.

114
00:07:25,216 --> 00:07:26,384
Right?

115
00:07:26,926 --> 00:07:28,219
She's holding an orange.

116
00:07:28,302 --> 00:07:29,679
You're right.

117
00:07:29,762 --> 00:07:31,514
-Midori!
-What?

118
00:07:31,597 --> 00:07:33,933
I found a <i>yukata </i>in the storage room.

119
00:07:34,016 --> 00:07:35,643
So cute! It's so retro.

120
00:07:35,726 --> 00:07:37,687
Try it on.
Must be a keepsake from your grandma.

121
00:07:37,770 --> 00:07:39,146
-I'll help you put it on.
-Really?

122
00:07:39,689 --> 00:07:41,691
Well, maybe I'll wear it then.

123
00:07:43,317 --> 00:07:46,237
It won't split at all. One more try!

124
00:07:46,320 --> 00:07:49,615
It won't split at all.
Is the angle the problem here?

125
00:07:49,699 --> 00:07:51,951
Do I have to strike it at this angle?

126
00:07:52,034 --> 00:07:55,288
-I can't do it.
-That's too weak! Stronger!

127
00:07:55,371 --> 00:07:57,957
-It's scary, Konta!
-Put your back into it!

128
00:07:58,040 --> 00:07:59,250
-Okay.
-Try it.

129
00:07:59,333 --> 00:08:01,127
That's no good.

130
00:08:01,210 --> 00:08:03,379
-Konta…
-Do it like, "Bam!"

131
00:08:03,462 --> 00:08:05,172
Focus! Like that.

132
00:08:05,798 --> 00:08:07,133
-I can't do it.
-You need to yell!

133
00:08:07,216 --> 00:08:08,050
Mr. Nishigami.

134
00:08:08,134 --> 00:08:09,010
Oh, Mr. Nishigami.

135
00:08:09,093 --> 00:08:12,096
See, Tetsuro is totally terrible at it,
so go teach him.

136
00:08:12,179 --> 00:08:13,556
-Yes.
-Okay.

137
00:08:13,639 --> 00:08:16,601
-I can't do it at all.
-We need firewood for the send-off fire.

138
00:08:17,435 --> 00:08:18,811
Ta-da!

139
00:08:18,894 --> 00:08:21,272
Oh! So cute!

140
00:08:21,355 --> 00:08:24,442
-Yay!
-So cute!

141
00:08:27,570 --> 00:08:30,281
-Thank you.
-My sister is so cute.

142
00:08:30,865 --> 00:08:32,992
-How is she so cute?
-Really, thanks.

143
00:08:33,075 --> 00:08:34,869
<i>From 5:00 p.m.,</i>

144
00:08:34,952 --> 00:08:38,164
<i>the Tatsumi Town</i>
<i>Summer Festival will begin…</i>

145
00:08:38,247 --> 00:08:39,498
Summer festival?

146
00:08:39,582 --> 00:08:42,793
<i>-Please do come and enjoy.</i>
-It's <i>Obon</i>, so maybe an <i>Obon </i>festival?

147
00:08:43,586 --> 00:08:46,547
It's held around this time every year.

148
00:08:46,631 --> 00:08:49,592
Really? I would like to go.
Where is it being held?

149
00:08:51,802 --> 00:08:53,846
Shall I guide you?

150
00:08:53,929 --> 00:08:55,931
Huh? Oh! Please do!

151
00:08:56,599 --> 00:08:57,892
Let's all go together.

152
00:08:57,975 --> 00:09:00,144
I don't want that monk
to yell at me again.

153
00:09:00,227 --> 00:09:01,103
We'll stay here.

154
00:09:01,187 --> 00:09:02,188
What?

155
00:09:02,271 --> 00:09:03,481
Go and have fun!

156
00:09:04,190 --> 00:09:05,650
Well, I'll go take a quick look.

157
00:09:05,733 --> 00:09:06,984
-Have fun.
-Okay!

158
00:09:07,068 --> 00:09:09,278
-I'm going too…
-No, not you.

159
00:09:09,362 --> 00:09:10,655
-You've got to chop wood.
-What?

160
00:09:10,738 --> 00:09:13,366
Hey, the two of them left together.

161
00:09:13,449 --> 00:09:16,077
A festival, huh. We only have one <i>yukata</i>.

162
00:09:16,160 --> 00:09:17,203
Yeah.

163
00:09:17,286 --> 00:09:20,539
-All right, let's prepare for <i>Obon</i>!
-Yeah.

164
00:09:20,623 --> 00:09:22,166
Let's set up the welcoming fire.

165
00:09:22,249 --> 00:09:23,584
Yay.

166
00:09:23,668 --> 00:09:25,336
Good, Tetsuro. Harder!

167
00:09:25,419 --> 00:09:26,879
Yes, right on!

168
00:09:39,475 --> 00:09:42,228
It was a small festival,
but it even had food stalls.

169
00:09:42,311 --> 00:09:43,688
It was fun.

170
00:09:44,397 --> 00:09:46,982
Next time,
I hope I can come with everyone.

171
00:09:47,817 --> 00:09:51,487
There are many different events
during <i>Obon</i>, aren't there?

172
00:09:52,446 --> 00:09:53,489
There sure are.

173
00:09:54,073 --> 00:09:57,243
The <i>Obon </i>holidays
are the only time working adults

174
00:09:57,326 --> 00:09:59,370
get to have a long summer holiday.

175
00:10:00,246 --> 00:10:04,041
I'm glad I got to have
a Japanese-style vacation.

176
00:10:04,125 --> 00:10:05,042
Ms. Midori.

177
00:10:05,126 --> 00:10:05,960
Yes?

178
00:10:06,043 --> 00:10:08,087
Shall we stop by one more place?

179
00:10:08,838 --> 00:10:09,672
What?

180
00:10:14,719 --> 00:10:17,012
MAIN GATE

181
00:10:28,983 --> 00:10:30,234
Wow.

182
00:10:38,242 --> 00:10:40,161
Please wait a moment.

183
00:11:11,066 --> 00:11:12,234
Could this be…

184
00:11:12,776 --> 00:11:14,069
My Grandma's?

185
00:11:16,989 --> 00:11:20,034
Ms. Nobuko really loved this town.

186
00:11:21,202 --> 00:11:22,286
Can I…

187
00:11:23,329 --> 00:11:24,747
take this back with me?

188
00:11:26,332 --> 00:11:27,249
Uh…

189
00:11:28,125 --> 00:11:32,171
I think Grandma would be happier
if we kept them in the villa.

190
00:11:33,255 --> 00:11:35,841
It's <i>Obon</i>, after all.
I will take them back.

191
00:11:38,010 --> 00:11:39,053
Hold on.

192
00:11:46,602 --> 00:11:48,979
It's been a while. Has it been a year?

193
00:11:49,063 --> 00:11:52,316
-Your grandchild, I think he got married?
-That's right!

194
00:11:52,942 --> 00:11:54,568
I can rest easy now.

195
00:11:54,652 --> 00:11:57,071
GHOSTS

196
00:11:57,154 --> 00:11:58,489
Mr. Nishigami.

197
00:11:58,989 --> 00:12:00,699
It has been a year.

198
00:12:00,783 --> 00:12:03,619
Mr. Nishigami,
thank you for the other day!

199
00:12:05,287 --> 00:12:06,288
Let's go.

200
00:12:06,372 --> 00:12:08,415
Did you get a girlfriend?

201
00:12:08,999 --> 00:12:10,292
Mr. Nishigami.

202
00:12:11,794 --> 00:12:13,837
-Mr. Nishigami.
-Come on!

203
00:12:21,387 --> 00:12:22,930
I'm very sorry.

204
00:12:23,013 --> 00:12:26,350
Oh, no, please don't apologize.

205
00:12:29,562 --> 00:12:32,147
Oh, thank you very much.

206
00:12:33,315 --> 00:12:37,695
This way
Grandma can return to the villa too.

207
00:12:40,322 --> 00:12:41,615
I knew it.

208
00:12:41,699 --> 00:12:44,451
These kinds of events
are important, aren't they?

209
00:12:45,202 --> 00:12:46,287
From next year,

210
00:12:46,370 --> 00:12:49,123
I'll be sure to give her
a much warmer welcome.

211
00:12:49,832 --> 00:12:51,000
Next year…

212
00:12:51,875 --> 00:12:54,587
-By <i>Obon </i>next year…
-Oh, <i>dango</i>!

213
00:12:56,088 --> 00:12:59,508
For <i>Obon</i>,
we make offerings of <i>dango</i>, right?

214
00:13:01,760 --> 00:13:06,265
Next year,
I will make <i>dango </i>for my Grandma.

215
00:13:09,893 --> 00:13:10,894
But…

216
00:13:11,979 --> 00:13:13,522
It's strange, isn't it?

217
00:13:14,356 --> 00:13:16,650
When I was working in Tokyo,

218
00:13:17,568 --> 00:13:21,071
I never paid <i>Obon </i>any mind.

219
00:13:21,739 --> 00:13:25,743
Well, I only cared how many days
of <i>Obon </i>holiday I could get.

220
00:13:26,619 --> 00:13:27,661
But…

221
00:13:27,745 --> 00:13:29,288
Even when I got time off,

222
00:13:30,539 --> 00:13:33,542
I would just be sleeping at home
or looking at my smartphone.

223
00:13:34,501 --> 00:13:37,296
Since coming here,

224
00:13:38,213 --> 00:13:41,925
I've realized that I was living
a rather bland life in Tokyo.

225
00:13:42,009 --> 00:13:43,302
I know that now.

226
00:13:44,845 --> 00:13:49,016
I was always tired,
and there was nothing I wanted to do.

227
00:13:52,394 --> 00:13:54,813
-Is that so?
-Yeah.

228
00:13:55,981 --> 00:13:57,775
Even my late grandma,

229
00:13:58,776 --> 00:14:03,405
<i>I hadn't seen her in years,</i>
<i>so I never really thought about her.</i>

230
00:14:07,117 --> 00:14:10,329
But, thanks to this villa,

231
00:14:10,996 --> 00:14:12,790
thanks to this vacation,

232
00:14:13,540 --> 00:14:16,502
<i>I was able to get in touch</i>
<i>with my precious memories.</i>

233
00:14:17,878 --> 00:14:19,505
<i>I found them again.</i>

234
00:14:21,840 --> 00:14:24,134
I'm glad I decided to take this vacation.

235
00:14:25,594 --> 00:14:27,137
Is that so?

236
00:14:30,599 --> 00:14:32,810
I'm glad I met you, Mr. Nishigami.

237
00:14:50,160 --> 00:14:53,288
I'm home, Mr. Nishigami.

238
00:15:27,448 --> 00:15:29,199
Grandma, welcome back.

239
00:15:29,283 --> 00:15:30,743
It has been a while,

240
00:15:30,826 --> 00:15:31,827
<i>Mr. Nishigami.</i>

241
00:15:31,910 --> 00:15:34,955
At the end of summer,
a great typhoon will come,

242
00:15:35,039 --> 00:15:36,415
and there will be a landslide.

243
00:15:36,498 --> 00:15:37,583
Oh, dear!

244
00:15:37,666 --> 00:15:39,752
<i>Will they all die?</i>

245
00:15:39,835 --> 00:15:42,504
Let me talk with them!

246
00:15:42,588 --> 00:15:44,882
<i>There is nothing I can do.</i>

247
00:15:46,091 --> 00:15:48,635
<i>You all must leave this place.</i>

248
00:15:50,262 --> 00:15:51,722
What's wrong?

